{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.807890Z","id":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","body":{"detail":"Stopping the daemon on exit hangs on AppLifecycleState.detached (runtime close, then supervisor.stop()), which is asynchronous; nothing holds the process open for it. Launching the debug app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME set to a scratch directory and stopping it with SIGTERM left the embedded clax (its PID from <support>/clax-home/daemon.json) running, and it had to be stopped by PID. DaemonSupervisor stops a daemon.json daemon whose /healthz answers with its PID before the next start (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart), so the next launch recovers; until then the daemon holds its port and CLAX_HOME. Whether Cmd-Q delivers detached in time is unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"2d7228ff0c61c7ee1b84b86a0b4c20e4ba42692f9520c81a978b4e4c6a0a71e8"},"suggested_fix":"On macOS, answer applicationShouldTerminate with terminateLater in AppDelegate.swift, ask Dart over the native channel to stop the worker and the supervisor, then reply to the app.","summary":"A macOS quit or a killed app process can leave the daemon running until the next launch","tags":["needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.807991Z","id":"db08c1245a167956dbe7823f1f5bac180303c9bc8395a3ca4d33e4360f9eaecd","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 7 has the WebView reload once a restarted daemon is up, so _AppPage reloads the surface when the endpoint's PID changes. The shell's own event stream reconnects by itself on the same port, so the reload only matters when the page's state went stale; it also discards a composer the person was typing into, and the page's scroll position unless the shell restores it. Reloading only when the shell does not report ready again within a short while would keep the draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":517},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"001e3f1ba895d304c889685fc43746a9bb0a245499e84ebeb16f0fbb08b565e5"},"summary":"A daemon restart on the same port reloads the open app, dropping an unsent composer draft","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.808034Z","id":"e6695aa01ca6e7647778a9d1ebf51e56e2dcec7bee3a22a9a16f506ccc633958","body":{"detail":"AgentRuntime stops the FeedbackWorker on Failed, which cancels the running change through AgentRequest.cancelled; recovery runs it again from the thread once Restart brings the daemon up. A model call that was nearly done is discarded. Keeping the worker running through Failed would let the result publish once the daemon is back, at the cost of polls failing (with backoff up to 10 s) until Restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"c29baf4b0608cc6a7e82f93ce31e00e5cc00ff6782d89986a1a0a9cd96cfb96a"},"summary":"A failed daemon cancels the change in flight, so its model run is paid again after Restart","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T11:59:38.617363Z","id":"34743c995d3d880cd783eb65f75e319b0f37cbe1d2a1fd93803d73b53f0cd1a3","body":{"detail":"Failure: quit the macOS app the ordinary way (Cmd-Q, Clax > Quit, or the AppleScript quit event; closing the last window takes the same path through applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed). The app process exits and its clax child keeps running, reparented to launchd, holding its port and CLAX_HOME until the next launch kills it. Reproduced twice against a debug build of e51b5922 (flutter build macos --debug) launched with CFFIXED_USER_HOME set to a scratch directory: osascript -e 'tell application \"<path>/clax_app.app\" to quit' ended the app (PIDs 1346 and 9232) and left clax (1970 and 9246) running with PPID 1; ps after five more seconds still listed it. The relaunch did stop 1970 through daemon.json, so the leak lasts until the next launch. The quit relies on AppLifecycleState.detached, whose handler starts an asynchronous runtime close and supervisor stop that nothing waits for. The osascript reply was error -128 (User canceled): FlutterAppDelegate answers applicationShouldTerminate with a cancel and hands the request to Dart as System.requestAppExit, so the framework's WidgetsBindingObserver.didRequestAppExit hook is called on this path and can hold the quit until the stop finishes.","kind":"blocker","references":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"2d7228ff0c61c7ee1b84b86a0b4c20e4ba42692f9520c81a978b4e4c6a0a71e8"},"suggested_fix":"Override didRequestAppExit in _AppRootState: await _runtime.close(), then await _s.supervisor.stop() (bounded by its SIGTERM-then-SIGKILL grace), then return AppExitResponse.exit. Test it with tester.binding.handleRequestAppExit() in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart, asserting the supervisor's stopCalls is 1 before the response is exit. Keep the detached path for Android.","summary":"Quitting the macOS app normally leaves the embedded daemon running","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:58.242908Z","id":"65e509cc146a8ee25f8c745eb40ad05efc1af12cd091430bd284341a6bbb51d7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3b5c19c","summary":"AppRoot.didRequestAppExit (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) stops the worker (2 s limit) and then the supervisor (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL; 5 s limit) before answering exit; detach shares the same once-only shutdown, and AppDelegate.applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed already returns true, so closing the last window takes the same path. Test 'quitting the app stops the worker and the daemon first' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart passes (flutter test: +418 ~3 skipped, All other tests passed). Live: flutter build macos --debug, launched the app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME=target/flutter-app/f9-home2 (app PID 35746, daemon PID 36209 from clax-home/daemon.json), ran osascript 'tell application id \"dev.empathic.clax\" to quit': the app exited and kill -0 36209 reported the daemon gone.","supersedes":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:58.243325Z","id":"9ec4b682111096624035b79e455173c94be72b34cda6dbc442c85f9ea80fd7e7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3b5c19c","summary":"AppRoot.didRequestAppExit (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) stops the worker (2 s limit) and then the supervisor (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL; 5 s limit) before answering exit; detach shares the same once-only shutdown, and AppDelegate.applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed already returns true, so closing the last window takes the same path. Test 'quitting the app stops the worker and the daemon first' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart passes (flutter test: +418 ~3 skipped, All other tests passed). Live: flutter build macos --debug, launched the app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME=target/flutter-app/f9-home2 (app PID 35746, daemon PID 36209 from clax-home/daemon.json), ran osascript 'tell application id \"dev.empathic.clax\" to quit': the app exited and kill -0 36209 reported the daemon gone.","supersedes":"34743c995d3d880cd783eb65f75e319b0f37cbe1d2a1fd93803d73b53f0cd1a3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122975Z","id":"a4f13018445ff96dcf721803a039a3bbe9583c77f4b266465aca02c9afa4b624","body":{"detail":"The notification follows MakeStage labels for a make and a fixed 'Working on your comment' for a change. AgentLoop.newApp takes onProgress and the worker emits WorkerProgress (lib/agent/worker.dart:27), but neither is passed to BackgroundRuns.step yet; _onWorker ignores WorkerProgress. Wire a short text from them (for example the size of the page written so far) with _runs.step(run, text).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"e1f97f681e6e08136cf0804ce6d60450068f2a57662275f4abcab8db172f7354"},"summary":"The background notification's progress text is only the making stage; streamed progress is not shown","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.809488Z","id":"836ff72799bb4c958c710b34be6a3d99af195c465e62d7e400e8501f356c8fa0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: lib/app.dart steps the make's and each change's BackgroundRun with progressStep (the latest Narration or ToolStarted label) from newApp's onProgress and from WorkerProgress. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart: 'a make shows its narration and tools in the notification, then opens the app', 'a change shows its narration in the notification'. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"a4f13018445ff96dcf721803a039a3bbe9583c77f4b266465aca02c9afa4b624","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.814816Z","id":"1e60b9dd6740e8fa3af86895562b252ab0729fca6883ae81e18e815e7a0c9eb7","body":{"detail":"AgentRuntime stops the FeedbackWorker on Failed, which cancels the running change through AgentRequest.cancelled; recovery runs it again from the thread once Restart brings the daemon up. A model call that was nearly done is discarded. Keeping the worker running through Failed would let the result publish once the daemon is back, at the cost of polls failing (with backoff up to 10 s) until Restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"e20425a31dc499f287202bd7fac1a475ffd1b2826f73351f3e21f112f08facf3"},"summary":"A failed daemon cancels the change in flight, so its model run is paid again after Restart","supersedes":"e6695aa01ca6e7647778a9d1ebf51e56e2dcec7bee3a22a9a16f506ccc633958","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.815553Z","id":"16065304e8eab625b90a381011139ac6d8cef828f150ec11c0d1f44b6423a497","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 7 has the WebView reload once a restarted daemon is up, so _AppPage reloads the surface when the endpoint's PID changes. The shell's own event stream reconnects by itself on the same port, so the reload only matters when the page's state went stale; it also discards a composer the person was typing into, and the page's scroll position unless the shell restores it. Reloading only when the shell does not report ready again within a short while would keep the draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":937},"end":{"line":952},"content_hash":"fb1d2536c137cd71b52cfbfa3de58ed3c97d8aed3e107879ed4604d777f84c70"},"summary":"A daemon restart on the same port reloads the open app, dropping an unsent composer draft","supersedes":"db08c1245a167956dbe7823f1f5bac180303c9bc8395a3ca4d33e4360f9eaecd","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.819321Z","id":"7405e1efac450d08971f4c769b7924fcaab0f3508a491d21f05076ad3cbae48b","body":{"detail":"usesToolLoop (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) chooses the tool loop when an inspector is given and the settings' backend takes turns (MessagesApiBackend) or AppServices.runner is set (the debug build's ScriptedRunner from a {\"runs\": …} CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT file). Once U6 passes its WebViewInspector, the worker's and the making screen's runs go through toolLoopRunner (MessagesApiRunner over ResumingTurns on AppServices.clock) with FileAskedQuestions('<support>/asked.json') (already passed by lib/main.dart) and AppServices.readConsent for U6's consent dialog.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"8acffa2fbea63204d0f0c69a86ef326c14e84d1e0314b54002ed36dba2bd9103"},"summary":"For Task U6: the tool loop runs only with AppServices.inspector; lib/main.dart passes none yet, so every run of the running app still takes the single structured call","tags":["handoff","task:U6","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:04.859954Z","id":"a649dc69ccefe6ffbb82d0603682eda2741ce0e9a2d7af8e3738b40ba60792df","body":{"detail":"AppRoot._aimed sends OpenThread once the shell's threads message lists the thread, which selects it in the page (its pin and card). The app screen's own thread page, with the reply and Retry, opens only from the panel (AppScreen._openThread in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart). An AppScreen parameter such as initialThread, opening ThreadDetail after the first ready, would land the person on the reply itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":941},"end":{"line":972},"content_hash":"068865621760b0d52560bb1f7d20da639591d7b4c95d77d451e888a569d0856e"},"summary":"An inbox reply opens its app and asks the shell to select the thread (claxHost.openThread); it does not open the app screen's thread page (ThreadDetail)","tags":["inbox","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
